# Curator environment variable reference
#
# Native ComfyUI mode configures paths and AI settings through the Curator
# page's header Settings modal (persisted as <curator system-user dir>/config.json).
# The variables below are fallbacks for native mode and the primary
# configuration for the CLI (curate.py).
#
# Native mode does NOT load .env files: set these variables in ComfyUI's own
# process environment (service unit, container environment, or a shell export
# before launching ComfyUI) when you want them used as fallbacks. curate.py does
# load .env through python-dotenv, so a copy of this file affects CLI runs only.
#
# See README.md for documentation and MIGRATION.md for standalone-to-native
# migration notes. NOTE: ~ in env-var values is NOT expanded by Python's pathlib.

# --- Paths ---
# Root directory for batch storage (inbox, shortlisted, finals, rejects).
# Native default (no Settings value and no env var): <curator system-user dir>/batches
# CLI default: ~/image-curator/batches
# Use an absolute path, or leave commented to use the entry point's default.
# IMAGE_CURATOR_BATCHES=/home/user/image-curator/batches

# Optional import source for images generated outside the batch library.
# Used by the native Import All workflow (set it in Settings for the normal
# path). The CLI never imports: curate.py only scores images already inside a
# batch folder. Most users can leave this unset and save/copy images into:
#   <batch-root>/<batch-name>/inbox/
# Native default: ComfyUI's own output directory
# IMAGE_CURATOR_COMFYUI=/home/user/image-curator/comfyui-outputs

# Optional safe root for copying/moving generated public posting copies out of
# batch-local public/ folders. Destinations entered in the UI must stay under
# this root. Native default: <curator system-user dir>/public-exports; change it
# in Settings. The CLI does not use this variable.
# IMAGE_CURATOR_PUBLIC_EXPORTS=/home/user/image-curator/public-exports

# The active batch pointer is not configurable by environment. Native mode
# stores it in <curator system-user dir>/state.json, and the CLI does not use a
# state file.
#
# IMAGE_CURATOR_BATCHES is shared by both entry points. IMAGE_CURATOR_COMFYUI,
# IMAGE_CURATOR_PUBLIC_EXPORTS, and IMAGE_CURATOR_THUMBNAIL_DELAY_MS only affect
# native mode. The AI variables below apply to both.

# --- Typed media (optional) ---
# FFmpeg executable for GIF/MP4 hover proxies and MP3/MP4 embedded-art posters.
# Default: ffmpeg (resolved from PATH). Use an absolute path when it is not on PATH.
# Missing FFmpeg is non-fatal: stable fallback posters remain available.
# IMAGE_CURATOR_FFMPEG=/usr/bin/ffmpeg

# Optional artificial delay (integer milliseconds) applied by both thumbnail
# adapters before serving, for degraded-condition benchmark runs. 0/unset disables.
# IMAGE_CURATOR_THUMBNAIL_DELAY_MS=0

# --- AI scoring (optional) ---
# URL of the OpenAI-compatible vision LLM endpoint (e.g. llama-swap, llama.cpp server)
IMAGE_CURATOR_LLM_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Model name/alias to request from the LLM server.
# Required for AI scoring. Must match a model configured on your LLM server.
# Accepts a comma-separated list (e.g. "vl-scorer,qwen-vl") to populate a
# dropdown in the UI; the first entry is the default selection.
IMAGE_CURATOR_MODEL=

# Request timeout in seconds for AI scoring
IMAGE_CURATOR_TIMEOUT=120

# Optional API key for the vision LLM endpoint. Sent as a Bearer token in the
# Authorization header. Leave empty or unset to skip authentication.
# Only required if your llama-swap / llama.cpp server enforces auth.
# Native mode prefers the Settings modal: stored keys are never returned by the
# settings API, and this variable is only a fallback.
# IMAGE_CURATOR_API_KEY=

# --- Network ---
# Curator has no host/port settings: it is served by ComfyUI's HTTP server.
# Use ComfyUI's own options instead, for example:
#   python main.py --listen 127.0.0.1 --port 8188
